/*
    resources/vulkan_kernels.comp -- Precompiled Vulkan utility kernels

    Each kernel is a section of this file that is compiled separately with
    '-D<NAME>' and the entry point '<name>', and the resulting modules are
    linked into a single module with one entry point per kernel (see the
    'vulkan' target of the Makefile).

    The kernels access memory through device addresses, and receive their
    parameters as push constants. The workgroup size is specialization constant
    0, and threads process the elements in a grid-stride loop.

